{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And behold, the skin of his face was radiant.</b> The kinds of light are divided: there is the light of wisdom, and there is the light that emerged from darkness. The light of wisdom is the light through which all was created, and it is what our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded regarding it: that it had already existed before the decree 'let there be light' preceded it, and it is what is called ראשית; and this light Moses attained in his heart, and through it he was distinguished from the rest of the prophets and exalted above all of them. The light that emerged from darkness is the elemental fire; it is what is called perceived light, and it is what came upon Moses so that the skin of his face became radiant. And the distinction of the radiance (qaran) that he now merited through the second tablets — which he did not merit through the first tablets, when it says 'and Moses turned and went down from the mountain' — is because all Israel were present there at the giving of the Torah for the first tablets, and all were witnesses to the matter through what they saw with their own eyes; but here, with the second tablets, concerning which he was warned (Exodus 34): 'and no man shall come up with you,' He gave him the distinction of radiance so that it would be a sign to Israel concerning the giving of the Torah. Or we may say that Moses was worthy of the radiance of the skin of the face even from the first tablets, and he was already established in the eyes of all Israel as a prophet of HaShem who would not need a sign with them; but because it was revealed and known before Him, blessed be He, that the first tablets were destined to be shattered, therefore He delayed this distinction for him until the second tablets, which endure." "<b>And they were afraid to approach him.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: How great is the power of sin! For before Israel sinned, they would see through the glory seven partitions of fire and not tremble, as it is said (Exodus 24:17): ״ומראה כבוד ה' כאש אוכלת בראש ההר לעיני בני ישראל״." "<b>And it is.</b> This phrase has seven words, corresponding to the number of the partitions that were לעיני בני ישראל; and when they sinned, they could not even look upon the face of the intermediary, as it is said: וייראו מגשת אליו." "<b>And behold.</b> Moses merited the rays of light from the cave, from what is written (Exodus 33): ״והיה בעבור כבודי ושמתיך בנקרת הצור״ — from the cleft of the rock he merited the radiance of the skin of his face; and so it says (Habakkuk 3:4): ״קרנים מידו לו ושם חביון עוזו״. And thus it is alluded to that from the tablets came the radiance of the skin of his face, in the manner of what is written (Ecclesiastes 8:1): ״חכמת אדם תאיר פניו״." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> והנה קרן עור פניו — all the splendor that Moses received in this world was nothing but the fruits of the giving of its reward, but the radiance endures for him in the world to come, as it is said: ״קרנים מידו לו״. End quote." "<b>And it appears to me</b> in explanation of this: that the קרן (radiance) — when his face was like the face of the sun, which is the fruits in this world — was like the fruit that falls from the tree; but in the world to come, the קרן abides for him as the light of the sphere above; it is the illuminating speculum (aspaklaria ha-me'irah), and this is what they said: 'the light of above wilts the orb of the sun.' And the Midrash makes the word קרן encompass both the קרן (ray) and the fruits."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {5 "The phrase 'נובלת אור של מעלה גלגל חמה' is opaque; read hyper-literally as printed. The apparent subject-switching between third-person (his face) and the rabbinic citation is preserved as in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:07:16.026247445Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}